From 5c5d4d91a1bf49b180e0c5c8012dd9fbbd64ca37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:21:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 133/140] Refactor lifecycle handling and improve download
 functionality

- Removed unnecessary lifecycle event observers from FileSystemBrowserScreen, MediaLibraryContent, MusicLibraryContent, VideoListScreen, and other components to streamline lifecycle management.
- Implemented coroutine-based refresh logic in MediaLibraryViewModel to react to media library changes.
- Enhanced download handling in NetworkStreamingScreen and PlayLinkSheet by utilizing coroutines for enqueueing downloads, improving responsiveness.
- Introduced a new DownloadThumbnail composable to display thumbnails for downloads in DownloadsScreen, enhancing UI consistency.
- Updated YtdlpManager to improve asset copying and installation checks, ensuring better error handling and logging.
- Added permission state tracking in PermissionUtils to handle permission grants more effectively.
